      "6(b)(ii) Refreshment purchases = payments $15,200 + closing creditors $2,170 − opening creditors $5,500 = $11,870. Cost of refreshments sold = $1,000 + $11,870 − $6,250 = $6,620. Trading profit = $25,800 − $6,620 = $19,180.",
      "6(b)(iii) Income: subscriptions $23,440 + refreshment profit $19,180 + raffle profit ($4,200 − $400) = $46,420. Expenses: groundsman $4,000 + sales girl $3,000 + utilities ($8,000 + $345) + rent ($12,000 − $300) + equipment depreciation (($20,000 + $12,600) × 10% = $3,260) = $30,305. Surplus = $16,115. If the sales girl's wages are charged within the refreshment trading account instead, its profit becomes $16,180 and no second $3,000 deduction is made; the total surplus is unchanged.",
